    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "The new date-override branch in checkIfIsAvailable intends to treat a zero-length override as a special case, but it compares dayjs(date.start).add(...) === dayjs(date.end).add(...). Since Dayjs instances are objects, this is an identity comparison, not a value comparison. Equal instants will still be different objects, so the zero-length override path is not taken and the slot is evaluated as if the override were not zero-length.",
      "confidence": 0.7200000286102295,
